FINAL ANSWER:
No one on the history is active. Every author has been silent for more than 6 months, so this file is orphaned. Pick reviewers by who understands the logic, not by line ownership.

- **Ignore the blame leader.** Fiona Formatter owns 89.9% of lines, but only because of the reformat commit `62628c0` (2026-04-12, 4-space indent and double quotes). It says nothing about who knows the logic.
- **Troy Goode is the best first choice.** They wrote the original file in 2013 and still own 8.4% of the lines. They also made the most recent real change, `b2005d9` "annotate handlers" (2026-04-10). Their last commit is about 6 months ago, so they may still respond.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson is the second choice.** Their 2017 commits cover the subtle CORS logic:
  - `075c4b5`: `Vary: Access-Control-Request-Headers`
  - `d603fdc`: the options delegate missing `methods`
  - `53405aa` and `00ce63a`: lint fixes
  - They have not committed since 2021-09-07, so check whether they are still reachable.
- **Others are unlikely to help.** Alejandro Caravaca Puchades wrote the array/regex `origin` matching (2015). Their commits are old, but they are a candidate if you touch that part.

Which area of `lib/index.js` are you changing? If you tell me, I can match it to the right person. Without a reachable reviewer, review it yourself and run the full test suite, especially the `Vary` header and preflight tests.

